    "recommendations": "Establishing clear address marking visible from the street could improve responder navigation, particularly given the extended driveway and single access point serving the property. Ensuring the driveway surface remains passable for emergency vehicles and that any vegetation encroaching along its edges does not reduce clearance width or overhead clearance would support faster apparatus access. Because rear access to the main building appears limited, pre-identifying any secondary pedestrian pathways that could support hose deployment or personnel movement around the structure may assist responders during operations. Confirming that address numbers are posted at both the street frontage and near the primary entrance could further reduce navigation delays upon arrival."
